INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,status,url_slug,created_at,updated_at) VALUES
('shinkan','Shinkan','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"shinkan","name":"Shinkan","team":"townsfolk","ability":"If you die at night, all evil players are drunk the next day and night.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"二礼二拍手一礼.","lede":"The Shinkan punishes evil for killing them by dulling their powers.","howToRun":["Remember that the Shinkan''s ability, if active, lasts for the next day and night. The evil team is not drunk on the night the Shinkan dies, so any other effects that night work as intended."],"tips":["As would be the case with any \"demon-bane\" roles, consider claiming strong information roles to bait a kill at night. Evidence of your existence is largely provable, especially with \"loud\" Minions and Demons such as the Al Hadikhia, Arbiter or Vizier: if their abilities don''t work, then you did! As such, you are reasonably well confirmed, as well as having been a boon to the good team."],"bluffing":["Bluffing as the Shinkan does require some level of \"sacrifice\" on your team''s behalf, as it will require them to act inactive. A Poisoner poisoning a dead body, a Fearmonger not changing their pick, the Cerenovus self-maddening, etc. Additionally, the Demon has to not kill on the corresponding night. However, this is an extremely powerful bluff, as there is some degree of mechanical confirmation around the Shinkan''s ability, so simulating it in full lends a lot of credence to the bluff."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Maddie is the Shinkan. They die on Night 3. The next day, the Psychopath attempts to kill the Empath, and it fails. The Psychopath is executed that same day.","Kamilla is the Hypnox claiming to be the Shinkan. They select themselves on Night 2. On Day 3, they inform their team and they coordinate a night and day of no evil impact."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":57.5,"otherNightReminder":"If the Shinkan has died tonight, mark all evil players as drunk.","reminders":["Drunk","Drunk","Drunk","Drunk","Drunk","Drunk"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/kang.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/kane.png"}','published','the-menagerie/shinkan',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('sleeper-the-menagerie','Sleeper','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"sleeper-the-menagerie","name":"Sleeper","team":"townsfolk","ability":"One Minion is drunk, and they learn this. You might register as an evil Minion.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"report day 2 STOP infiltration successful STOP no suspicion must lay low STOP do not rescue STOP destroy upon receipt STOP","lede":"The Sleeper goes deep into enemy lines, posing as a Minion in order to nullify an evil player''s ability.","howToRun":["This is a fairly dynamic character with a lot of fun interactions: the initial decision to make a Minion drunk impacts game balance, so consider having the Sleeper register as a Minion to give town reasons to push them out of the game, or out themselves."],"tips":["For as long as you are alive, you can be assured that while sober, an in play Minion is unable to function as intended. This should provide some assurance that, even though you aren’t able to out your role, you are providing a benefit to town, even if that puts you at risk. This is not information you can out to town freely, but if you are suspected of being a Minion yourself, you may consider outing your information and trying to take a Minion with you in the process. The Storyteller may not grant your wish, but at least you tried, no?"],"bluffing":["If you are a Minion bluffing as the Sleeper, it’s crucial that you abide by the rules of the character and stay quiet about a Sleeper being in play: not dying when revealing your role might give the game away! That said, having a Minion “malfunction” might sell a world where you really exist, and may curry the town’s favour, even if they won’t want to push on the how or why. Then, when the time is right, you can spring to life and cause terror in town. You may now be outed as an evil player, but in a diminished town that can’t afford to waste time getting rid of you."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Ethan is the Sleeper. The Poisoner is told that they are made drunk, but neither state as much to their respective teammates. Ethan dies on Night 3 and the Poisoner regains their ability.","Josh is the Imp bluffing as the Sleeper. Josh suggests that they believe the Marionette - which is not in play - has been \"slept\", and therefore the Demon wouldn''t know who they are, leading good players to question their alignment."],"firstNight":7.5,"firstNightReminder":"Select a Minion and give them the ‘Slept’ reminder token . Inform that Minion that a Sleeper is in play.","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":["Slept"],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Baron","align":"good","text":"If the Baron is made drunk by the Sleeper, the Sleeper learns there is a Baron in play.","id":"baron"},{"name":"Marionette","align":"good","text":"If the Marionette is made drunk by the Sleeper, the Demon does not learn who they are.","id":"marionette"},{"name":"Evil Twin","align":"good","text":"If the Evil Twin is made drunk by the Sleeper, they are still paired with a good player, but the game does not end if the good player dies.","id":"eviltwin"},{"name":"Summoner","align":"good","text":"If the Summoner is drunk on the 3rd night, the Summoner chooses which Demon, but the Storyteller chooses which player.","id":"summoner"},{"name":"Vizier","align":"good","text":"If the Vizier loses their ability, they learn this. If the Vizier is executed while they have their ability, their team wins.","id":"vizier"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/sleg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/slee.png"}','published','the-menagerie/sleeper',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('smith-the-menagerie','Smith','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"smith-the-menagerie","name":"Smith","team":"townsfolk","ability":"On your first night, create an ability for yourself, agreed to by the Storyteller. The Demon learns a clue as to its nature.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"With fire and strength, I shape the world.","lede":"The Smith creates their own tools.","howToRun":["As with the Wizard, the Smith''s ability should be within the bounds of what would be considered fun and solvable. Use your discussion with the Smith to mediate this. Remember to wake the Smith and a point in the night appropriate to their ability, if at all.","Aim to steer away from abilities that are mechanically confirming in most cases, since they are often impossible to bluff by the evil team, but also confirm the Smith is what they claim.","While moderating an ability on the spot is difficult, consider aiming for something less powerful than what an Amnesiac might receive, given the distinct downside of the Amnesiac not knowing the ability they have."],"tips":["Unlike the Amnesiac, who has to figure out what their Storyteller-given ability is, you know right from the jump, because you create it yourself! Get creative, make up abilities that have never been seen before, or pick an off-script role to mimic. Remember that the Demon gains a clue as to what your ability might be, so information that you gain, or effects your ability might trigger can be easily discerned by the evil team, or worse, copied, so be judicious."],"bluffing":["Evil roles have a lot of overlap with what a Smith might learn, so craft an ability that sounds plausible in order to prove yourself to be real. If you have a Devil''s Advocate, consider an ability that can protect. If you have a Poisoner, perhaps your ability learns powerful information at the expense of \"drunking\" players each night. Or if you have a Godfather, perhaps you can claim to have a power that can kill at night if an evil player dies during the day! You have far more mechanically confirmable abilities at your disposal than most good players, so bluffing as the Smith gives you free reign to reverse engineer tools at your disposal to fit the role."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Eric is the Smith. On Night 1, he proposes to gain the ability to learn characters killed by the Demon each night. The Storyteller agrees to this ability, and wakes the Demon to let them know that the Smith''s ability learns about Demon kills.","TJ is the Fang Gu with the Boffin Gossip ability. They gossip a true statement during the day, but claim they are in fact the Smith, who gains the ability to kill during the night if a player who is drunk or poisoned is executed during the day. Fun!"],"firstNight":45,"firstNightReminder":"The Smith proposes an ability. It can be agreed to or negotiated. Wake the Demon and provide a hint as to the nature of the agreed ability.","otherNight":16,"otherNightReminder":"If applicable, wake the Smith at a point in the night appropriate to their ability.","reminders":["1","2","3","4","5"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/smig.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/smie.png"}','published','the-menagerie/smith',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('swindler-the-menagerie','Swindler','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"swindler-the-menagerie","name":"Swindler","team":"townsfolk","ability":"Once per game, at night*, receive a good player''s info and three players that may have sent it. That info is wrong for both players.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Ho there - yes, you in the dirty apron! You look like a lucky fella. And you, miss! You with those lovely scissors in hand! Something tells me luck is on your side this fine day. Don''t be scared, I don''t bite. Now, watch closely as I place the ball under the cup...","lede":"The Swindler steals a copy of another good player''s information, but corrupts it in the process.","howToRun":["The Swindler’s power can be moderated on the basis of how well town is doing. If they are doing well, consider picking a character whose information is difficult to immediately parse, and vice versa. It may also be worth including evil players in the three that are ‘seen’ by the Swindler, as they may be inclined to share the information they received. If there are no remaining information roles in play, the Swindler’s power simply fails - but this in itself is also useful information.","Be sparing with first night roles: corrupting their information can be harmful to town, but puzzling out the correct information can ultimately be helpful."],"tips":["Your job as the Swindler is to confirm another player around the Grimoire. The cost, of course, is that you corrupt the information that Townsfolk receives, so there is some wisdom, perhaps, in calling out your role once used to see if you can determine where that information came from. Some information, like the Dreamer’s, is quite obvious, while others are much broader or general, so the difficulty in figuring out the source varies. With that said, the ability to confirm another player outside of the first day is extremely powerful, and the understanding that the information is necessarily wrong (rather than poisoned) means you can potentially puzzle out a correct answer along with your swindled ally. There is even an argument to make your discussion extremely obvious, since if you manage to gather the information of a spent role such as a Seamstress, you can goad the Demon into killing them under the impression that they may be something ongoing."],"bluffing":["As a confirmation role, this is a really powerful bluff for the evil team. Given that the information received by the Swindler is wrong, you don’t need to lean too heavily on your knowledge of the town to ensure that your role is legitimised. Use your ‘ability’, confirm a team-mate - be they the Demon or a Minion who will likely become the Demon - and don’t put up a fight if you’re nominated. You are, after all, a spent role!"],"fighting":[],"examples":["Scott is the Swindler. He uses his ability at night, receiving a yes. The three players he receives are the Fortune Teller, who received a no; the Flowergirl, who received a yes; and the Town Crier, who also received a yes.","Kevin is the Poisoner bluffing as the Swindler. He poisons the Oracle overnight, and claims to receive what he believes to be an incorrect Oracle number. The three players he claims to receive are the Oracle, the Chambermaid, and the Artist."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":57.5,"otherNightReminder":"From Night 2: Wake the Swindler and ask if they wish to use their ability. If they do, when a player of your choice receives info tonight, it is wrong: send a copy of that info to the Swindler. If no info is left to send, the Swindler learns nothing.","reminders":["Swindled","Wrong","Wrong","No Ability"],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Spy","align":"good","text":"The Spy may register to the Swindler’s ability.","id":"spy"},{"name":"Vortox","align":"good","text":"If a Vortox is in play, the Swindler produces and receives correct information.","id":"vortox"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/swing.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/swine.png"}','published','the-menagerie/swindler',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('thaumaturge-the-menagerie','Thaumaturge','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"thaumaturge-the-menagerie","name":"Thaumaturge","team":"townsfolk","ability":"Each night, choose a player. The first Minion ability that targets this player targets that Minion instead. Affected Minions learn you are 1 of 2 players.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Fie, fie I say! Back to whence you came, foul minion!","lede":"The Thaumaturge can turn a Minion''s powers back against them.","howToRun":["You can moderate the Thaumaturge’s impact on the game by who you provide in the ping if a Minion is successfully bounced. If the Thaumaturge’s team needs some assistance, consider framing the same two people frequently, and if evil team is doing poorly, spreading around the wrong ping will help pin down the source."],"tips":["Finding prime targets for Minion abilities will enable you to get the best value out of your role. As characters like the Monk protect certain characters from the Demon, your job is to protect characters from the Minion, with the bonus that a “bounced” ability will cause interesting, unintended consequences. And, of course, if no good targets present themselves, you can always target yourself. Once your ability is triggered, the evil team will be on your trail, and the chance of being found out increases, so get as much value out of your ability as possible."],"bluffing":["If you’re a Minion that has an ability that targets other players, you can bluff as the Thaumaturge to frame other players: pick unusual targets to simulate a bounce, and claim you targeted other, more obvious targets. Keep in mind, of course, that if the player you frame is executed, you’ll need to figure out a way forward with your ability still intact - but if you’re expendable, consider requesting that your Demon take you out of play to sell the lie."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Steven is the Thaumaturge who chooses the Cannibal. The Cerenovus also chooses the Cannibal at night, making themselves mad in the process. The Cerenovus learns that Steven and one other player is the Thaumaturge.","Amy is the Godfather bluffing as the Thaumaturge. They kill the Sage at night, claiming to have selected the Devil''s Advocate. Despite further Outsider deaths at night, there are no extra night deaths. Amy suggests that the Sage may have been the Godfather whose kill bounced via the Thaumaturge''s ability."],"firstNight":6.5,"firstNightReminder":"The Thaumaturge chooses a player. If any Minion ability targets them, inform the Minion that they are targeted instead. Inform that Minion that the Thaumaturge is the corresponding player and one wrong player.","otherNight":6.5,"otherNightReminder":"The Thaumaturge chooses a player. If any Minion ability targets them, inform the Minion that they are targeted instead. Inform that Minion that the Thaumaturge is the corresponding player and one wrong player.","reminders":["Safe","Thaumaturge","Wrong"],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Assassin","align":"good","text":"The Assassin is unaffected by the Thaumaturge''s ability, but still learns the two players that might be the Thaumaturge.","id":"assassin"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/thag.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/thae.png"}','published','the-menagerie/thaumaturge',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('wire-tapper','Wire Tapper','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"wire-tapper","name":"Wire Tapper","team":"townsfolk","ability":"On Night 1, if you use your ability, the Demon learns one in-play character as part of their bluffs, and 1 Townsfolk is drunk until dusk. The Demon learns you are in play.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"... .-.. .- -.-- . .-. .-.-.- / ... --- .-.. -.. .. . .-. .-.-.- / -- .- -.-- --- .-. .-.-.- (Creator credit: Matt)","lede":"The Wire Tapper corrupts lines of communication, mixing up their Demon bluffs - or not.","howToRun":["Select an in-play role as you would an out-of-play role as the Demon’s corrupted bluff; however take some care when selecting the player to drunk as a result of the Wire Tapper’s power; choosing the ‘wrong’ person may have unintended consequences for the game, and more importantly, render some roles like ‘you start knowing’ roles redundant without any interference from another player such as the Poisoner. Consider drunkening ongoing information roles, something that might cause some drama early on, or - if the game state heavily favours evil - someone who isn’t impacted by it at all."],"tips":["This is a Townsfolk with a binary choice on the first night, but it is an incredibly powerful one! Whether you use your ability or not, the Demon learns that you exist, and so you may choose to use it to toss an in-play role into their bluffs, or decline to ensure town stays as sober as possible. But no matter what you choose to do, the Demon cannot be 100% certain that their bluffs will hold! Use this to your advantage and either claim to be the Wire Tapper early, or perhaps hold on to it and sniff out any double claims; they may just be evil in (a poor) disguise."],"bluffing":["Given the Wire Tapper’s ability, this is an easy role to bluff, but sadly your utility only goes as far as the first day. If you are a powerful Minion with a ‘spent’ teammate such as the Baron, you may consider asking them to fall into a double claim to legitimise yourself, and gain trust with town which can keep you alive and operational. Just know that a Wire Tapper who is reluctant to be fed to the Vortox, for instance, may not be terribly trustworthy."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Lavender is the Wire Tapper who chooses to use their ability. The Demon receives three roles - the Mechanical Man, the Evangelist, and the Slayer - one of which is an in-play role.","Jessie is the Boffin bluffing as the Wire Tapper. They have given their Demon the Librarian''s ability, and are fed to the Vortox that afternoon. Such is life. However, the two players claiming Fortune Teller - one the real Fortune Teller, the other the Pixie, are pushed on by town for a double claim, potentially due to the Wire Tapper''s ability."],"firstNight":15,"firstNightReminder":"The Wire Tapper may use their ability. If they say yes, replace a Demon bluff with an in-play character (not the Wire Tapper). Mark one Townsfolk as Wires Crossed.","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":["Bluff","Wires Crossed"],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Snitch","align":"good","text":"If the Snitch is in play, one Minion bluff is also affected by the Wire Tapper: no additional Townsfolk are made drunk.","id":"snitch"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/wirg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/wire.png"}','published','the-menagerie/wire-tapper',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('barfly','Barfly','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"barfly","name":"Barfly","team":"outsider","ability":"On your first day, you must publicly guess 5 players'' characters (not including yourself or Travellers). If the majority are incorrect, one player is drunk from now on, even if you are dead.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Ey, ''ey you there... you''re the wazscherwoman, yeah? The Zzaint? Oh, schorry about that. Get a lil''... a lil''... *hic* - ''ey, ''ey you - the unnertaker, aye-- oh, bugger it: barkeep! Wassail for all! (Creator credit: Twindels)","lede":"The Barfly socialises immediately to learn who''s who, with dire consequences if they don''t get it quite right.","howToRun":["Use the Barfly''s drunkening the same way you might a Sweetheart''s. Remember that characters like the Recluse and Spy might misregister."],"tips":["Under construction!"],"bluffing":["Under construction!"],"fighting":[],"examples":["Will is the Barfly. On Day 1, he guesses 5 players'' roles, getting 2 correct. The Artist, as a result, is immediately drunk.","Hugo is the Godfather bluffing as the Barfly. On Day 1, he guesses members of his evil team among his 5 players, and the Mathematician learns a 0 overnight."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":["Incorrect","Incorrect","Incorrect","Incorrect","Incorrect","Drunk"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/barg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/bare.png"}','published','the-menagerie/barfly',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('blasphemer','Blasphemer','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"blasphemer","name":"Blasphemer","team":"outsider","ability":"The first Townsfolk you speak to privately becomes a not-in-play Outsider if you die. If you die without speaking to a Townsfolk, or if all Outsiders are in play, another player might die that night.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Alas, my wounds are mortal. With my dying breath, I cast thee out!","lede":"The Blasphemer turns a welcome Townsfolk to a reviled Outsider, but might discover hidden evil in the process.","howToRun":["Make sure you mark the Blasphemer’s first conversation with a Townsfolk, and keep that reminder token in play until the Blasphemer’s death. Remember that the Blasphemer’s ability doesn’t affect Outsiders, Minions or Demons."],"tips":["You know how your ability operates, and so there is a valid fear that you may turn a valuable Townsfolk into a potentially detrimental Outsider when you die. As such, track your conversations and warn whoever you speak to from the outset of the game that they are now burdened with your ability. Of course, the upside is that if the player you warn doesn’t turn into an Outsider, but someone reports being turned instead, you can be reasonably assured that your first conversation was with an evil player, or a Drunk! Though you’ve negatively impacted your team, you now have a piece of valuable information that will help solve the game.","Given your unique situation, you may choose to only interact with confirmed Outsiders, or people who are willing to risk being turned. The obvious downside is that your information will be (mostly) second hand, and it will be difficult to gain an understanding in the same way that other players might, but at the same time, you help to confirm those players upon your death. If possible, you may also want to consider killing the Blasphemer on a day when their ability is misfiring: if you discover that they are poisoned or drunk in some way, whether by a Minstrel, Courtier, or Minion ability, take that opportunity to safely dispatch the Blasphemer. Of course, there is also the option of simply not engaging in any private conversations, but that carries its own downside: how you choose to play the Blasphemer, then, is up to you."],"bluffing":["If you have a Pit Hag, consider changing a Townsfolk into an Outsider when a high-value Townsfolk dies. This may cast doubt on that player’s information, and may also help to steer people away from believing that a Pit Hag is in play. Additionally, if you know the Outsider count is high, turning someone into the Blasphemer ensures an additional death at night.","If you choose to play as the Blasphemer yourself, consider \"outing\" to someone trustworthy and let them know of your situation. This may make town reluctant to kill you, lest they lose access to a powerful Townsfolk role, and may also give your team information about precisely who you’ve chosen to target. You can also claim, perhaps, that your Demon will be transformed into an Outsider, which may carry its own negatives."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Gul is the Blasphemer. He speaks with two players on the first day. The second player Gul speaks to, upon their death, turns into the Saint. The first player that Gul spoke to is the Drunk or evil.","Ben is the Godfather claiming to be the Blasphemer. He speaks with his Demon on Day 1, and later claims, upon his execution, that the Demon has become the Plague Doctor."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":57.5,"otherNightReminder":"If the Blasphemer has died today or tonight, wake the Townsfolk marked ''Doomed'' and show them the YOU ARE token . Assign them a not-in-play Outsider character.","reminders":["Doomed","Turns Tonight","Dead"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/blag.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/blae.png"}','published','the-menagerie/blasphemer',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));